{
  "case_id": "2010-09-525",
  "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: MARK A. PERRY, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of Petitioners. DAVID C. FREDERICK, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of Respondent. CURTIS E. GANNON, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Affirming the judgment below would authorize private securities fraud class actions against every service provider that participates in the drafting of a public company's prospectus. It is, therefore, nothing less than a frontal assault on this Court's decisions in Central Bank and Stoneridge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, is -- who's the violator alleged here? Not in the complaint, but in the briefs? As I read the briefs, they claim that Janus itself did not make the false statement, that the two appellants did, that they are the actual speakers because they were talking about their activities, and they used Janus as a conduit to deceive the market."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Well, somebody deviated from what was the announced policy, that there was to be no market timers investing in this -- in these Janus funds. Somebody made the decision that certain hedge funds would be allowed to engage in that activity. Who was that somebody?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Perry",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "These funds are managed -- \"governed,\" excuse me, is a better word -- by the trustees. That is disclosed in"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You're not suggesting, are you, that they did this for purposes of protecting your client from a lawsuit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "hypothetical you gave where the president gives an innocent board of directors false information and the prospectus goes out, is the company liable because their agent -- is the company liable under 10b-5?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, this case -- this case went off on -- in the district court, it was -- was it 12(b)(6)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They didn't have substantive control over the content of the message, because if they did, they would not have allowed these false statements to have been issued."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Curtis E. Gannon",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0002-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A primary violator must be somebody who has actually committed all the elements of a 10b-5 cause of action -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm interested in your test. I'm interested in your test, not the -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Curtis E. Gannon",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0002-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The control person liability also needs to have a primary violator under the terms of 20(a)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Mr. Gannon)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GANNON: Well, I think the easiest way would be to analogize it to the cases involving corporate employees. As Petitioners acknowledge, there are cases where a corporate employee drafts a statement that's issued in the company's name. In this instance, the investment adviser is management for the company, and the fact that they happen to be management by virtue of contract rather than just the internal arrangements of the corporation shouldn't change that arrangement. It -- it's also the case that if the Court were -- were looking for a way to narrow its holding, it could do so by talking about the elements of the 10b-5 cause of action, which -- which would apply only to private suits and -- and not to enforcement actions brought by the Commission or by the Department of Justice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Your point is that -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Mr. Perry)",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PERRY: If it is a dupe case, Justice Ginsburg and Justice Sotomayor, it's dealt with by 20(b), which Justice -- Mr. Gannon did not answer. You'll notice 20(b) does not require a primary violation. It allows the Commission to proceed directly against any person who acts indirectly where it can't act directly. So 20(b) answers this problem."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Perry, on the allegations of this complaint, these plaintiffs were harmed by the misrepresentations, the alleged misrepresentations from JCM to the fund."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44d2d06a12e14e2b95ef5ee6d9905bb9147c15a3c05c06889c735fb29d4d0158",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44d2d06a12e1-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, Mr. Perry. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
